WEBVTT

00:00:12.190 --> 00:00:15.810
One hundred years have passed
since the Battle of Galluah Plains,

00:00:15.810 --> 00:00:19.150
where King Kyle defeated
the Dark Lord Angmund.

00:00:19.150 --> 00:00:22.600
The Demons rise again,
threatening the world

00:00:22.600 --> 00:00:26.020
and spreading fear and unrest to all.

00:00:26.020 --> 00:00:30.400
If it's so tough, you should just run.

00:00:30.400 --> 00:00:34.900
You need to live for yourself.
Otherwise, your heart will die.

00:00:34.900 --> 00:00:38.980
Through meeting Reina,
Kasel is able to shake free from his fears

00:00:38.980 --> 00:00:42.190
to activate the power of the Holy Sword.

00:00:42.190 --> 00:00:45.600
They now approach the Windland
Snow Mountains,

00:00:45.600 --> 00:00:48.600
to meet Pavel, who can unlock the final seal.

00:00:49.650 --> 00:00:53.310
I won't run... Never!

00:00:54.230 --> 00:00:59.100
<i>When the red-stained night comes</i>

00:00:59.100 --> 00:01:04.310
<i>I paint you on the sky</i>

00:01:04.830 --> 00:01:14.720
"KING's RAID:
Successors of the Will"

00:01:15.350 --> 00:01:19.190
<i>The hidden truth</i>

00:01:19.190 --> 00:01:23.730
<i>The sudden suffocation</i>

00:01:25.230 --> 00:01:28.980
<i>You are so distant, fading</i>

00:01:28.980 --> 00:01:33.650
<i>Do you feel it too?</i>

00:01:33.650 --> 00:01:35.980
<i>Crossing blades</i>

00:01:35.980 --> 00:01:38.810
<i>Cannot touch</i>

00:01:38.810 --> 00:01:43.440
<i>The sadness that lies beyond</i>

00:01:43.440 --> 00:01:45.940
<i>I just want to see you</i>

00:01:45.940 --> 00:01:49.900
<i>I search for you</i>

00:01:49.900 --> 00:01:53.310
<i>Now, Eclipse</i>

00:01:53.310 --> 00:01:58.230
<i>I always want to be by your side</i>

00:01:58.230 --> 00:02:00.900
<i>I send a wish to the sky</i>

00:02:00.900 --> 00:02:03.100
<i>I believe in destiny</i>

00:02:03.100 --> 00:02:05.520
<i>When the sun and moon meet</i>

00:02:05.520 --> 00:02:07.980
<i>At that moment</i>

00:02:07.980 --> 00:02:11.190
<i>I run to you</i>

00:02:11.190 --> 00:02:15.060
<i>With all my heart</i>

00:02:23.910 --> 00:02:28.910
<i></i>A Night of

00:02:23.910 --> 00:02:28.910
<i></i>Reminiscing

00:02:32.690 --> 00:02:36.270
We're just one seal away from
completely unleashing the Holy Sword!

00:02:36.270 --> 00:02:38.810
Finally getting close!

00:02:38.810 --> 00:02:41.600
I wonder what Master Pavel is like?

00:02:41.600 --> 00:02:45.520
He's a hero who fought alongside
King Kyle 100 years ago!

00:02:45.520 --> 00:02:49.060
I'm sure he's a super powerful sorcerer!

00:02:49.060 --> 00:02:52.230
Oh, I can't wait to meet him!

00:02:52.230 --> 00:02:53.810
Stay sharp.

00:02:53.810 --> 00:02:56.190
I know!

00:02:56.190 --> 00:02:59.560
The Windland Snow Mountains
are just up ahead. Let's hurry.

00:02:59.560 --> 00:03:00.940
Yes.

00:03:07.350 --> 00:03:08.770
An undead!

00:03:19.020 --> 00:03:22.060
Undead? Here...?

00:03:29.270 --> 00:03:31.150
What's wrong, Roi?

00:03:32.440 --> 00:03:34.690
It's nothing. Let's go.

00:03:55.480 --> 00:03:57.400
I'll take watch now.

00:03:58.810 --> 00:04:00.400
Yeah...

00:04:00.400 --> 00:04:02.600
What's wrong, Roi?

00:04:02.600 --> 00:04:03.940
About what?

00:04:03.940 --> 00:04:07.270
You seem different somehow.

00:04:12.230 --> 00:04:15.480
I was remembering something.

00:04:15.480 --> 00:04:19.650
Now that you've mentioned it,
I haven't heard about your past at all.

00:04:19.650 --> 00:04:21.230
Really?

00:04:21.230 --> 00:04:22.600
Yeah.

00:04:22.600 --> 00:04:26.270
I used to be part of a group of mercenaries.

00:04:39.270 --> 00:04:41.770
Hey, kid, you alive?

00:04:42.940 --> 00:04:45.400
You dead? Hey.

00:04:46.310 --> 00:04:49.600
Hey, you're alive.

00:04:49.600 --> 00:04:51.230
Leave me alone.

00:04:51.230 --> 00:04:52.560
Huh?

00:04:52.560 --> 00:04:55.400
I said, leave me alone.

00:05:05.810 --> 00:05:10.690
Hey, slow down. That's bad for your digestion.

00:05:10.690 --> 00:05:13.850
You haven't eaten anything for a while, right?

00:05:15.350 --> 00:05:17.270
Hey, someone's here.

00:05:17.270 --> 00:05:20.730
Did you find a new one again, Captain?

00:05:22.190 --> 00:05:23.440
Captain?

00:05:23.440 --> 00:05:25.600
I forgot to tell you.

00:05:25.600 --> 00:05:29.980
I'm Zayed. I'm the captain of
a group of mercenaries.

00:05:29.980 --> 00:05:31.900
Speaking of which, what's your name?

00:05:31.900 --> 00:05:34.690
Huh? You haven't even asked his name yet?

00:05:35.690 --> 00:05:39.190
It's Roi. I will repay this debt soon.

00:05:39.190 --> 00:05:41.060
Don't worry about it.

00:05:41.060 --> 00:05:43.400
No, I will, for sure.

00:05:43.400 --> 00:05:47.020
Then why don't you join us, Roi?

00:05:48.150 --> 00:05:51.230
Become a member of Flugel!

00:05:57.270 --> 00:05:59.190
Why am I doing this...?

00:05:59.190 --> 00:06:00.810
Roi!

00:06:00.810 --> 00:06:04.020
When you're done over there,
come help over here!

00:06:05.150 --> 00:06:10.350
I thought you guys were mercenaries.
Why are you doing these things?

00:06:10.350 --> 00:06:15.230
"These things"? Helping those
in need is totally part of our job!

00:06:15.230 --> 00:06:18.350
Huh? Mercenaries are supposed
to fight for money.

00:06:18.350 --> 00:06:22.650
I'd say we're more like helping hands.

00:06:22.650 --> 00:06:24.400
Indeed!

00:06:25.600 --> 00:06:29.150
All of you, get in here and eat something!

00:06:29.150 --> 00:06:31.310
That smells so good!

00:06:31.310 --> 00:06:36.100
I've got you my special soup.
Eat up and work hard.

00:06:36.100 --> 00:06:38.350
Thanks, old lady!

00:06:38.350 --> 00:06:40.270
"Old lady"...?

00:06:40.270 --> 00:06:44.440
There's no old lady here. I'm the Madam!

00:06:44.440 --> 00:06:46.100
Remember that, kid!

00:06:46.100 --> 00:06:47.940
Uh, yeah...

00:06:47.940 --> 00:06:51.900
So, who's the new kid?

00:06:51.900 --> 00:06:53.980
Just a new stray dog!

00:06:53.980 --> 00:06:55.900
Who're you calling stray dog?

00:06:55.900 --> 00:07:00.100
You were collapsed on the street
from hunger. What's the difference?

00:07:03.980 --> 00:07:06.980
He would accept any job.

00:07:06.980 --> 00:07:11.850
I couldn't understand
what he was thinking, at all.

00:07:11.850 --> 00:07:14.440
I was still a kid back then.

00:07:17.310 --> 00:07:22.730
I will never understand why
we must use thugs like you, but...

00:07:22.730 --> 00:07:28.190
My master specifically asked for you,
so here I am. Be grateful.

00:07:28.190 --> 00:07:30.560
Yes, most certainly sir.

00:07:30.560 --> 00:07:34.230
Besides, I don't approve of you.

00:07:34.230 --> 00:07:38.770
If it wasn't for my master,
you all wouldn't have such an easy life.

00:07:38.770 --> 00:07:40.730
Indeed, that is correct.

00:07:40.730 --> 00:07:45.350
I suppose being disposable is a value.

00:07:45.350 --> 00:07:49.020
We will do our best to perform
above your expectations.

00:07:49.020 --> 00:07:54.730
Please call on us again
if you have another opportunity.

00:07:54.730 --> 00:07:58.850
Remember that you're always replaceable.
I expect no less than your best.

00:07:58.850 --> 00:08:00.310
Yes.

00:08:05.690 --> 00:08:09.100
Why are you letting him
talk to you like that?!

00:08:09.100 --> 00:08:11.400
Why are you so mad?

00:08:11.400 --> 00:08:14.810
Will you grovel to someone like that
if the money is good?

00:08:14.810 --> 00:08:19.270
That's right, because there are
more important things in life.

00:08:20.400 --> 00:08:27.310
I've got to raise you kids.
I'll do anything for that.

00:08:27.310 --> 00:08:29.060
When I do something, I go all the way!

00:08:29.060 --> 00:08:30.440
What does that even mean?

00:08:32.690 --> 00:08:34.600
Stop treating me like a child!

00:08:34.600 --> 00:08:36.230
Sorry, sorry.

00:08:36.230 --> 00:08:38.810
All right! Let's grab something to eat!

00:08:39.850 --> 00:08:41.900
What was that...?

00:08:41.900 --> 00:08:46.230
The Captain lost his family a while ago.

00:08:46.230 --> 00:08:49.770
Some things happened,
and he ended up making this group, Flugel.

00:08:49.770 --> 00:08:53.100
The Captain found us too, like you.

00:08:53.100 --> 00:08:56.270
It must have been tough enough for him
to make a living just for himself.

00:08:56.270 --> 00:08:59.650
But he got us a place to live
and took care of us.

00:08:59.650 --> 00:09:03.650
That's why we're willing to do
anything for the Captain.

00:09:03.650 --> 00:09:06.020
It's the least we could do, honestly.

00:09:10.520 --> 00:09:12.650
What are you doing?

00:09:12.650 --> 00:09:14.600
You wanna study, too?

00:09:14.600 --> 00:09:15.560
Huh?

00:09:15.560 --> 00:09:17.480
Captain, hurry!

00:09:17.480 --> 00:09:19.770
What are you going to teach us today?

00:09:19.770 --> 00:09:22.190
Yeah, one sec.

00:09:22.190 --> 00:09:24.980
Why study?

00:09:24.980 --> 00:09:26.850
You know, Roi...

00:09:26.850 --> 00:09:33.100
In this world, there are many who want
to study but can't, for various reasons.

00:09:33.100 --> 00:09:36.310
Everyone has their own stories.

00:09:36.310 --> 00:09:38.980
I can't change the world by myself.

00:09:38.980 --> 00:09:42.650
But I can teach some things.

00:09:42.650 --> 00:09:47.150
Who knows what difference it would make
to be able to read and write?

00:09:47.150 --> 00:09:49.690
But one day, it will be useful.

00:09:49.690 --> 00:09:53.020
Isn't that what's called meddling?

00:09:53.020 --> 00:09:58.440
Maybe. But once I decide
to do something, I go all the way!

00:09:58.440 --> 00:10:00.810
All the way!

00:10:03.940 --> 00:10:05.440
He's a nice person.

00:10:05.440 --> 00:10:09.270
More like, a nosy weirdo.

00:10:09.270 --> 00:10:12.310
He had a symbol of a wing
embroidered on his sleeve.

00:10:12.310 --> 00:10:15.100
Its meaning is very
indicative of his personality.

00:10:15.100 --> 00:10:22.310
Dreams and hope become wings
to soar towards the future...

00:10:22.310 --> 00:10:26.150
He seriously said that's
the grand meaning behind the symbol.

00:10:26.150 --> 00:10:28.230
That's cool.

00:10:28.230 --> 00:10:30.060
I see...

00:10:31.810 --> 00:10:33.350
So...

00:10:33.350 --> 00:10:36.020
The undead from earlier today was...

00:10:36.020 --> 00:10:39.270
That was Pavian, one of the members.

00:10:40.310 --> 00:10:43.310
I didn't expect him to be out here...

00:10:43.310 --> 00:10:44.310
Roi...

00:10:44.310 --> 00:10:47.100
We all got split up in the Galluah Plains.

00:10:47.100 --> 00:10:48.690
Galluah Plains...

00:10:48.690 --> 00:10:52.980
One day, Orvelia sent us a terrible job.

00:10:52.980 --> 00:10:56.690
We were supposed to
investigate the Galluah Plains.

00:10:56.690 --> 00:11:02.520
They said nobody entered that place
after the battle 100 years ago.

00:11:02.520 --> 00:11:08.270
Of course, in reality, I'm sure many people
went in, but nobody came back.

00:11:08.270 --> 00:11:13.440
There had to be some reason why
they couldn't come back.

00:11:13.440 --> 00:11:16.520
But the Captain took up that offer.

00:11:16.520 --> 00:11:20.100
He believed in a future where a road
cutting through the Galluah Plains,

00:11:20.100 --> 00:11:24.310
safe for anyone to travel on, could be built.

00:11:31.940 --> 00:11:35.020
How far did Eddie go?

00:11:35.020 --> 00:11:37.480
He's taking way too long.

00:11:42.770 --> 00:11:45.770
I'll go find him. You all wait here.

00:11:45.770 --> 00:11:47.190
Hey, I'll go, too.

00:11:47.190 --> 00:11:50.980
No. It's quicker for me to go alone.

00:11:52.270 --> 00:11:55.100
If you say so, Captain...

00:11:55.100 --> 00:11:57.480
All right, be right back!

00:12:16.350 --> 00:12:18.600
When is the captain coming back...?

00:12:18.600 --> 00:12:21.100
Should we go check it out?

00:12:21.100 --> 00:12:22.270
We should!

00:12:22.270 --> 00:12:24.900
He told us to wait here.

00:12:24.900 --> 00:12:26.650
You want us to just sit around?

00:12:26.650 --> 00:12:30.480
The captain always thinks things through
before taking action.

00:12:30.480 --> 00:12:33.190
That's true, but...

00:12:33.190 --> 00:12:37.060
But if something were to happen to him...

00:12:37.060 --> 00:12:39.650
He's coming back for sure!

00:12:44.100 --> 00:12:47.190
I'm worried! Let's go look!

00:12:47.190 --> 00:12:48.400
I'll go, too!

00:12:48.400 --> 00:12:50.310
Hey, guys?!

00:13:02.900 --> 00:13:05.440
This really is a spooky place...

00:13:05.440 --> 00:13:07.690
Let's find them fast!

00:13:07.690 --> 00:13:08.980
Yeah!

00:13:09.900 --> 00:13:12.850
Isn't that the captain?

00:13:16.940 --> 00:13:18.940
Captain!

00:13:19.900 --> 00:13:23.270
Why did you come? I told you to wait!

00:13:23.270 --> 00:13:25.310
We couldn't wait any longer!

00:13:25.310 --> 00:13:28.810
We're so glad you're safe.

00:13:28.810 --> 00:13:31.600
We'll help find Eddie.

00:13:32.980 --> 00:13:35.440
You guys can be so stubborn!

00:13:45.940 --> 00:13:47.310
What?!

00:13:53.230 --> 00:13:54.770
Captain? Pavian!

00:14:04.480 --> 00:14:05.690
How's the captain?!

00:14:07.400 --> 00:14:09.190
What happened...?

00:14:09.190 --> 00:14:11.940
I don't know, but he's gone...

00:14:11.940 --> 00:14:13.480
Why?!

00:14:13.480 --> 00:14:16.150
Why the captain? Why Pavian?!

00:14:16.150 --> 00:14:17.350
Huh?

00:14:25.520 --> 00:14:26.850
What, you--

00:14:42.310 --> 00:14:44.730
R-Run! Run!

00:14:49.060 --> 00:14:52.150
Help! Captain!

00:14:58.520 --> 00:15:00.440
You're awake.

00:15:00.440 --> 00:15:02.150
Where am I?

00:15:02.150 --> 00:15:04.400
The Tower of the Sage.

00:15:04.400 --> 00:15:06.230
The Tower of the Sage?

00:15:06.230 --> 00:15:10.150
A sorcerer brought you here.

00:15:10.150 --> 00:15:12.600
I see... Thank you.

00:15:12.600 --> 00:15:15.850
What happened?

00:15:15.850 --> 00:15:18.480
I don't fully understand, but...

00:15:22.270 --> 00:15:26.350
I see. That is probably the undead.

00:15:26.350 --> 00:15:30.100
Undead... Is there any way
to bring them back?

00:15:30.100 --> 00:15:35.190
The undead are moving corpses.
There is no way to revive the dead.

00:15:35.190 --> 00:15:37.100
Moving corpses...

00:15:38.850 --> 00:15:40.440
Why did that happen...?

00:15:40.440 --> 00:15:44.230
It is the result of magics made
by a sorcerer named Malduk.

00:15:44.230 --> 00:15:45.770
Malduk?

00:15:45.770 --> 00:15:51.400
I don't know if Malduk is dead or still alive.

00:15:51.400 --> 00:15:55.900
A hundred-year-old trap? Or...

00:15:59.690 --> 00:16:04.230
I've done some research on the undead.

00:16:04.230 --> 00:16:08.480
This place is full of literature
and research results.

00:16:08.480 --> 00:16:12.440
You should study up on the undead
to your heart's content.

00:16:12.440 --> 00:16:14.520
Why do you care about me so much...?

00:16:14.520 --> 00:16:20.900
It's a trade. There is something
I need your help with.

00:16:35.190 --> 00:16:40.520
I see. So that's how you knew
so much about the undead.

00:16:40.520 --> 00:16:41.600
Yeah.

00:16:41.600 --> 00:16:49.060
Dominix had me stay at the Tower of the Sage
to make me travel with you, Kasel.

00:16:50.440 --> 00:16:55.600
I can't let Malduk continue whatever
he's doing, for my fallen friends.

00:16:55.600 --> 00:16:59.270
We have to get the Holy Sword
and take him out.

00:16:59.270 --> 00:17:00.690
Yeah!

00:17:00.690 --> 00:17:05.850
So. Enough stories. I'm going to sleep.

00:17:18.190 --> 00:17:20.730
Morning! Wake up, everyone!

00:17:20.730 --> 00:17:22.940
The weather is fine again today!

00:17:25.850 --> 00:17:27.440
Good morning.

00:17:27.440 --> 00:17:29.270
Good morning, Frey.

00:17:33.480 --> 00:17:34.900
Hey, Roi.

00:17:36.400 --> 00:17:39.400
If your old friend was here...

00:17:41.310 --> 00:17:45.520
...maybe your captain is nearby, too?

00:17:45.520 --> 00:17:46.770
Maybe.

00:17:46.770 --> 00:17:47.540
Then...!

00:17:47.540 --> 00:17:48.810
What's wrong?

00:17:48.810 --> 00:17:51.480
Yeah, what's with the secret talk?

00:17:54.060 --> 00:17:57.770
There could be more undead nearby.

00:17:58.730 --> 00:18:01.060
Huh? What do you mean?

00:18:05.190 --> 00:18:08.600
I see... I didn't know.

00:18:08.600 --> 00:18:12.980
But we've fought many undead before.

00:18:12.980 --> 00:18:16.900
Even if that undead appears...

00:18:16.900 --> 00:18:18.900
...can't we just take it out?

00:18:24.900 --> 00:18:29.190
The undead have physical strengths
far stronger than when they were alive.

00:18:29.190 --> 00:18:31.190
We can't underestimate them.

00:18:31.190 --> 00:18:36.940
If there's a risk of a surprise attack,
we should take it out before moving forward.

00:18:36.940 --> 00:18:39.270
But we don't have time to...

00:18:40.100 --> 00:18:43.560
I know! There's a way to find them quickly!

00:18:43.560 --> 00:18:45.150
Huh?

00:18:45.520 --> 00:18:50.770
They react to loud noises and voices.

00:18:52.060 --> 00:18:56.230
To lure out the undead, we just
have to make a really loud noise.

00:18:56.230 --> 00:18:58.230
But how?

00:18:58.230 --> 00:19:00.190
That's easy.

00:19:00.190 --> 00:19:01.400
There.

00:19:04.310 --> 00:19:07.310
Hey! Warn us before you do that!

00:19:10.690 --> 00:19:13.650
Good! They're not here!

00:19:13.650 --> 00:19:15.270
That doesn't justify anything!

00:19:20.520 --> 00:19:22.940
I'm sorry to get you all caught up in this.

00:19:22.940 --> 00:19:25.560
Don't mention it.

00:19:25.560 --> 00:19:31.020
My deal with Dominix isn't
the only reason I'm on this trip.

00:19:31.020 --> 00:19:34.730
Finding the captain and
dealing with him myself...

00:19:34.730 --> 00:19:37.440
That's always been one of my goals.

00:19:37.440 --> 00:19:38.850
Roi...

00:19:40.980 --> 00:19:43.150
Huh? What?

00:19:53.270 --> 00:19:55.060
Captain.

00:20:03.940 --> 00:20:06.100
Let's end this quick.

00:20:06.100 --> 00:20:07.560
Yeah...

00:20:14.270 --> 00:20:16.440
I'll lay you to rest!

00:20:36.230 --> 00:20:38.190
I'll handle this one!

00:21:26.560 --> 00:21:29.310
<i>This one wish</i>

00:21:29.310 --> 00:21:32.020
<i>Connects you and me</i>

00:21:32.020 --> 00:21:34.810
<i>I wait so impatiently for tomorrow</i>

00:21:34.810 --> 00:21:38.850
<i>Because I know you now</i>

00:21:50.270 --> 00:21:55.400
<i>A comfortable breeze passes over</i>

00:21:55.400 --> 00:22:01.270
<i>A memory in a precious place</i>

00:22:01.270 --> 00:22:05.940
<i>From the day I decided to walk with you</i>

00:22:05.940 --> 00:22:12.600
<i>The promise that I hid in my heart</i>

00:22:12.600 --> 00:22:18.060
<i>I want to feel that moment, just once</i>

00:22:18.060 --> 00:22:20.350
<i>If I stretch my arm out</i>

00:22:20.350 --> 00:22:23.730
<i>I should be able to reach</i>
<i>the tomorrow in my dream</i>

00:22:23.730 --> 00:22:26.400
<i>This one wish</i>

00:22:26.400 --> 00:22:29.270
<i>I gently engrave in my heart</i>

00:22:29.270 --> 00:22:32.020
<i>The chain that connects the heart</i>

00:22:32.020 --> 00:22:34.810
<i>Cannot ever be broken</i>

00:22:34.810 --> 00:22:37.600
<i>The future which we should head to</i>

00:22:37.600 --> 00:22:40.350
<i>Beckons us to come closer</i>

00:22:40.350 --> 00:22:43.190
<i>I wait so impatiently for tomorrow</i>

00:22:43.190 --> 00:22:46.150
<i>Because I know you now</i>

00:23:16.650 --> 00:23:20.520
I'll pick up where you left off.

00:23:29.440 --> 00:23:32.850
I'll try... doing it all the way.

00:23:47.150 --> 00:23:49.980
The cold winds blow hard along this path.

00:23:49.980 --> 00:23:55.310
An action taken to protect friends
leads to an unforeseen result.

00:23:55.310 --> 00:24:00.730
Each individual determination
shows us a new path.

00:23:58.330 --> 00:24:00.910
<i></i>Hidden

00:23:58.330 --> 00:24:00.910
<i></i>Determination
